# SQLite runs in WAL mode (README, Operational hardening), so these two
# sidecars exist beside the live ledger permanently -- and the -wal holds
# ledger pages not yet checkpointed into the .db. Only the e2e ones were
# listed, so basis.db-wal showed as untracked on the executor host, one
# `git add -A` away from committing trade data.
